1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,956
A token is a password for a program. Treat it like one.

2
00:00:04,506 --> 00:00:09,541
If it leaks, anyone can use it. And if it is too powerful, they can do a lot of damage.

3
00:00:10,091 --> 00:00:12,472
Today we make the Jenkins token small,

4
00:00:12,472 --> 00:00:14,289
so a leak is a small problem.

5
00:00:14,289 --> 00:00:15,416
Then we revoke it,

6
00:00:15,416 --> 00:00:16,732
watch the build fail,

7
00:00:16,732 --> 00:00:18,048
and put in a new one.

8
00:00:18,598 --> 00:00:21,691
Small token. Easy to revoke. Never in the code.

9
00:00:23,241 --> 00:00:24,670
Here is what to expect.

10
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:29,935
One: the three kinds of token in Sonar cube, and which one a pipeline should use.

11
00:00:30,485 --> 00:00:31,879
Two: the life of a token.

12
00:00:31,879 --> 00:00:32,827
Where it is made,

13
00:00:32,827 --> 00:00:33,886
where it is stored,

14
00:00:33,886 --> 00:00:35,392
and when it is thrown away.

15
00:00:35,942 --> 00:00:37,197
Three: a live demo.

16
00:00:37,197 --> 00:00:38,651
We make a small token.

17
00:00:38,651 --> 00:00:40,039
We prove it is small.

18
00:00:40,039 --> 00:00:41,493
We revoke the old one,

19
00:00:41,493 --> 00:00:42,815
and the build fails.

20
00:00:42,815 --> 00:00:45,128
Then we give Jenkins the new token,

21
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:46,054
and it passes.

22
00:00:46,604 --> 00:00:50,550
Four: project permissions, the mistakes that hurt, and the lab files.

23
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:54,279
This is objective seven of the Sonar cube domain.

24
00:00:55,829 --> 00:00:57,728
First, the three kinds of token.

25
00:00:58,278 --> 00:00:59,123
A user token.

26
00:00:59,123 --> 00:01:00,099
It acts as you,

27
00:01:00,099 --> 00:01:01,659
with all of your rights.

28
00:01:01,659 --> 00:01:03,480
If you are an administrator,

29
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:04,521
so is the token.

30
00:01:04,521 --> 00:01:06,341
Use it for your own scripts,

31
00:01:06,341 --> 00:01:07,707
never for a pipeline.

32
00:01:08,257 --> 00:01:09,919
A global analysis token.

33
00:01:09,919 --> 00:01:12,204
It can run a scan on any project,

34
00:01:12,204 --> 00:01:13,381
and nothing else.

35
00:01:13,381 --> 00:01:13,866
Better.

36
00:01:13,866 --> 00:01:14,974
But if it leaks,

37
00:01:14,974 --> 00:01:16,705
every project is exposed.

38
00:01:17,255 --> 00:01:18,885
A project analysis token.

39
00:01:18,885 --> 00:01:21,037
It can run a scan on one project,

40
00:01:21,037 --> 00:01:22,146
and nothing else.

41
00:01:22,146 --> 00:01:24,167
This is the one for a pipeline.

42
00:01:24,717 --> 00:01:29,666
The rule is called least privilege. Give a token the smallest power that does the job.

43
00:01:30,216 --> 00:01:31,768
Then add an expiry date,

44
00:01:31,768 --> 00:01:34,096
and a name that says what it is for.

45
00:01:34,096 --> 00:01:36,552
Jenkins dash CI tells you who uses it.

46
00:01:38,102 --> 00:01:39,745
Now, the life of a token.

47
00:01:40,295 --> 00:01:41,906
It is made in Sonar cube,

48
00:01:41,906 --> 00:01:43,259
on your account page.

49
00:01:43,259 --> 00:01:44,871
The server shows it once.

50
00:01:44,871 --> 00:01:46,417
It never shows it again.

51
00:01:46,967 --> 00:01:52,493
You store it in Jenkins credentials. Jenkins keeps it encrypted, and hides it in the logs.

52
00:01:53,043 --> 00:01:58,611
The pipeline asks for it by name, in the scan step. It is never typed in the Jenkinsfile.

53
00:01:59,161 --> 00:02:00,087
When it leaks,

54
00:02:00,087 --> 00:02:01,344
or a person leaves,

55
00:02:01,344 --> 00:02:02,999
or the expiry date comes,

56
00:02:02,999 --> 00:02:03,925
you revoke it.

57
00:02:03,925 --> 00:02:06,307
The old token stops working at once.

58
00:02:06,857 --> 00:02:08,428
Then you make a new token,

59
00:02:08,428 --> 00:02:09,999
and update the credential.

60
00:02:09,999 --> 00:02:11,509
The code does not change.

61
00:02:11,509 --> 00:02:13,684
That is the benefit of a credential.

62
00:02:15,234 --> 00:02:16,515
Let us do it.

63
00:02:16,515 --> 00:02:19,866
We open Sonar cube in the browser,

64
00:02:19,866 --> 00:02:24,300
and sign in as the administrator of this lab.

65
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:27,749
A token always belongs to a person,

66
00:02:27,749 --> 00:02:30,509
so we start from an account.

67
00:02:39,059 --> 00:02:40,496
We open our account,

68
00:02:40,496 --> 00:02:41,430
and Security.

69
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:44,591
This page lists every token of this account.

70
00:02:44,591 --> 00:02:45,309
Two exist.

71
00:02:45,309 --> 00:02:46,890
One is called jenkins.

72
00:02:46,890 --> 00:02:49,045
It is a global analysis token.

73
00:02:49,045 --> 00:02:51,560
This is the one Jenkins uses today.

74
00:02:58,110 --> 00:03:00,118
Now we make a smaller one.

75
00:03:00,118 --> 00:03:02,127
The name: jenkins dash CI.

76
00:03:02,127 --> 00:03:04,676
The type: Project Analysis Token.

77
00:03:04,676 --> 00:03:06,530
The project: Cloud Cart.

78
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:08,538
It expires in thirty days.

79
00:03:08,538 --> 00:03:09,929
We click Generate.

80
00:03:11,979 --> 00:03:13,968
Sonar cube shows the token once.

81
00:03:13,968 --> 00:03:14,962
We store it now,

82
00:03:14,962 --> 00:03:17,262
because it will never be shown again.

83
00:03:17,262 --> 00:03:19,064
We do not paste it in a file,

84
00:03:19,064 --> 00:03:19,872
or in a chat.

85
00:03:21,922 --> 00:03:23,342
Now a test of power.

86
00:03:23,342 --> 00:03:24,478
In the terminal,

87
00:03:24,478 --> 00:03:28,241
we ask the same administrator question to two tokens.

88
00:03:28,241 --> 00:03:30,513
The question: list the webhooks.

89
00:03:30,513 --> 00:03:32,289
First the analysis token,

90
00:03:32,289 --> 00:03:33,638
then my user token.

91
00:03:33,638 --> 00:03:35,768
The analysis token is refused.

92
00:03:35,768 --> 00:03:37,614
The user token is allowed.

93
00:03:37,614 --> 00:03:40,738
This is why a pipeline gets the small token.

94
00:03:42,288 --> 00:03:44,661
Now imagine the old token leaked.

95
00:03:44,661 --> 00:03:45,956
A laptop was lost,

96
00:03:45,956 --> 00:03:47,394
or a log was shared.

97
00:03:47,394 --> 00:03:48,329
We revoke it.

98
00:03:48,329 --> 00:03:49,696
Back in Sonar cube.

99
00:03:49,696 --> 00:03:52,069
Next to the token called jenkins,

100
00:03:52,069 --> 00:03:53,219
we click Revoke.

101
00:03:53,219 --> 00:03:54,298
And we confirm.

102
00:03:54,298 --> 00:03:55,521
It stops working,

103
00:03:55,521 --> 00:03:56,240
right now.

104
00:04:00,790 --> 00:04:02,972
Jenkins still has the old token.

105
00:04:02,972 --> 00:04:04,063
So what happens?

106
00:04:04,063 --> 00:04:05,495
We switch to Jenkins,

107
00:04:05,495 --> 00:04:06,313
and sign in.

108
00:04:06,313 --> 00:04:07,744
Then we open the job,

109
00:04:07,744 --> 00:04:09,040
cloud cart quality,

110
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,404
and click Build Now.

111
00:04:10,404 --> 00:04:11,631
The console opens,

112
00:04:11,631 --> 00:04:13,267
and we follow the build.

113
00:04:13,267 --> 00:04:15,108
We expect the scan to fail,

114
00:04:15,108 --> 00:04:17,835
because the token Jenkins holds is dead.

115
00:04:26,385 --> 00:04:26,980
The first stage,

116
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:27,537
build and test,

117
00:04:27,537 --> 00:04:28,466
does not need Sonar cube.

118
00:04:28,466 --> 00:04:29,246
It compiles the code,

119
00:04:29,246 --> 00:04:30,175
and runs the forty tests.

120
00:04:30,175 --> 00:04:30,695
And it passes.

121
00:04:31,245 --> 00:04:36,343
Look at the console. Maven runs the tests one by one, and every test is green.

122
00:04:36,893 --> 00:04:38,595
Then the Scan stage starts.

123
00:04:38,595 --> 00:04:41,999
It asks Jenkins for the credential called sonar token,

124
00:04:41,999 --> 00:04:43,827
and sends the report with it.

125
00:04:44,377 --> 00:04:45,795
But that token was revoked a minute ago.

126
00:04:45,795 --> 00:04:46,894
The Jenkinsfile did not change.

127
00:04:46,894 --> 00:04:48,276
Only the token behind the name is dead.

128
00:04:48,276 --> 00:04:49,198
Let us wait a few seconds.

129
00:04:49,748 --> 00:04:50,214
Failed.

130
00:04:50,214 --> 00:04:51,878
And the message is clear.

131
00:04:51,878 --> 00:04:52,677
Four oh one,

132
00:04:52,677 --> 00:04:53,543
Unauthorized.

133
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:55,074
Please check the token.

134
00:04:55,074 --> 00:04:58,403
The pipeline did exactly what we want: it stopped,

135
00:04:58,403 --> 00:04:59,668
and it told us why.

136
00:05:00,218 --> 00:05:02,095
The fix is not in the code.

137
00:05:02,095 --> 00:05:03,277
It is in Jenkins.

138
00:05:03,277 --> 00:05:04,320
Manage Jenkins,

139
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,154
Credentials,

140
00:05:05,154 --> 00:05:05,989
sonar token.

141
00:05:05,989 --> 00:05:07,866
We click Update credential.

142
00:05:07,866 --> 00:05:09,326
Then Change Password,

143
00:05:09,326 --> 00:05:11,621
because the old secret is hidden.

144
00:05:11,621 --> 00:05:13,637
We click in the secret field,

145
00:05:13,637 --> 00:05:15,306
and paste the new token.

146
00:05:15,306 --> 00:05:16,627
It shows only dots.

147
00:05:16,627 --> 00:05:17,183
We save.

148
00:05:17,183 --> 00:05:19,269
It is the only change we make.

149
00:05:24,819 --> 00:05:26,484
Now we run the job again.

150
00:05:26,484 --> 00:05:27,216
We open it,

151
00:05:27,216 --> 00:05:28,548
and click Build Now.

152
00:05:28,548 --> 00:05:30,213
Then we open the console,

153
00:05:30,213 --> 00:05:31,545
to follow the build.

154
00:05:31,545 --> 00:05:33,742
The credential now holds the new,

155
00:05:33,742 --> 00:05:34,675
smaller token.

156
00:05:42,225 --> 00:05:44,278
This time the scan is accepted.

157
00:05:44,278 --> 00:05:45,537
The token is small,

158
00:05:45,537 --> 00:05:49,777
but it has the one power we need: run an analysis on Cloud Cart.

159
00:05:50,327 --> 00:05:51,197
While it runs,

160
00:05:51,197 --> 00:05:52,441
look at the console.

161
00:05:52,441 --> 00:05:54,368
Jenkins never prints the token.

162
00:05:54,368 --> 00:05:56,234
If a command tried to show it,

163
00:05:56,234 --> 00:05:58,348
Jenkins would print stars instead.

164
00:05:58,898 --> 00:06:00,353
That is called masking.

165
00:06:00,353 --> 00:06:01,619
It protects the log.

166
00:06:01,619 --> 00:06:05,669
It does not protect the token from someone who can edit the job.

167
00:06:05,669 --> 00:06:08,263
So keep the right to edit jobs small too.

168
00:06:08,813 --> 00:06:12,278
A good habit: rotate tokens before the expiry date,

169
00:06:12,278 --> 00:06:13,840
one token for each job,

170
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:17,304
and revoke the token of anyone who leaves the team.

171
00:06:17,854 --> 00:06:20,051
And notice what we did not touch.

172
00:06:20,051 --> 00:06:21,116
The Jenkinsfile.

173
00:06:21,116 --> 00:06:21,716
The code.

174
00:06:21,716 --> 00:06:22,581
The pipeline.

175
00:06:22,581 --> 00:06:23,913
Only the credential.

176
00:06:24,463 --> 00:06:30,201
Green. All three stages. The gate passed. A new, smaller token, and nothing else changed.

177
00:06:30,751 --> 00:06:31,751
One more check.

178
00:06:31,751 --> 00:06:33,683
Is there a token in the code?

179
00:06:33,683 --> 00:06:34,882
We run leak check.

180
00:06:34,882 --> 00:06:36,282
No token in the code.

181
00:06:36,282 --> 00:06:38,414
The token is only in Sonar cube,

182
00:06:38,414 --> 00:06:40,479
and in the Jenkins credentials.

183
00:06:41,029 --> 00:06:41,375
Last,

184
00:06:41,375 --> 00:06:42,204
permissions.

185
00:06:42,204 --> 00:06:44,140
A token decides who you are.

186
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:46,697
A permission decides what you may do.

187
00:06:46,697 --> 00:06:48,356
In the project settings,

188
00:06:48,356 --> 00:06:49,808
the Permissions page.

189
00:06:49,808 --> 00:06:53,817
A person who only scans needs one thing: Execute Analysis.

190
00:06:53,817 --> 00:06:54,853
Not administer.

191
00:06:55,403 --> 00:06:58,155
Finally, the proof. Lab check. Four of four.

192
00:06:58,705 --> 00:07:00,837
The user token can administer.

193
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:02,542
The CI token is refused.

194
00:07:02,542 --> 00:07:04,033
No token in the code.

195
00:07:04,033 --> 00:07:06,023
And the last build is green.

196
00:07:07,573 --> 00:07:08,725
Five mistakes.

197
00:07:09,275 --> 00:07:15,078
One: using a user token in the pipeline. It carries all your rights. A leak is a disaster.

198
00:07:15,628 --> 00:07:17,656
Two: one token for everything.

199
00:07:17,656 --> 00:07:18,603
When it leaks,

200
00:07:18,603 --> 00:07:19,550
you revoke it,

201
00:07:19,550 --> 00:07:20,970
and every job breaks.

202
00:07:20,970 --> 00:07:22,796
Use one token for each job.

203
00:07:23,346 --> 00:07:28,636
Three: a token with no expiry date. It lasts for ever, and nobody remembers it.

204
00:07:29,186 --> 00:07:31,432
Four: a token in the Jenkinsfile,

205
00:07:31,432 --> 00:07:32,862
or in a chat message.

206
00:07:32,862 --> 00:07:34,019
Git remembers it,

207
00:07:34,019 --> 00:07:35,720
even after you delete it.

208
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:36,673
If it happens,

209
00:07:36,673 --> 00:07:37,762
revoke it first.

210
00:07:38,312 --> 00:07:41,941
Five: giving the pipeline user the administer permission,

211
00:07:41,941 --> 00:07:43,342
because it was easier.

212
00:07:43,342 --> 00:07:45,634
Give it Execute Analysis and Browse,

213
00:07:45,634 --> 00:07:46,398
and no more.

214
00:07:47,948 --> 00:07:50,743
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

215
00:07:51,293 --> 00:07:52,757
One: the repository,

216
00:07:52,757 --> 00:07:57,077
git hub dot com slash it dash waves slash dev ops dash A I,

217
00:07:57,077 --> 00:07:59,421
in the folder academy slash lab.

218
00:07:59,971 --> 00:08:05,539
Two: the files, lab one seventy dot S H, and shortcuts one seventy dot S H.

219
00:08:06,089 --> 00:08:07,934
Three: load the short names,

220
00:08:07,934 --> 00:08:10,701
with source shortcuts one seventy dot S H.

221
00:08:10,701 --> 00:08:11,887
You get lab check,

222
00:08:11,887 --> 00:08:12,546
try token,

223
00:08:12,546 --> 00:08:13,534
and leak check.

224
00:08:14,084 --> 00:08:15,870
Four: set Analysis token,

225
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:16,727
Sonar token,

226
00:08:16,727 --> 00:08:17,942
and Jenkins auth,

227
00:08:17,942 --> 00:08:18,871
as variables,

228
00:08:18,871 --> 00:08:20,228
to your own values.

229
00:08:20,228 --> 00:08:23,300
Never put them in a file in the repository.

230
00:08:23,850 --> 00:08:26,206
Five: make a project analysis token,

231
00:08:26,206 --> 00:08:27,384
prove it is small,

232
00:08:27,384 --> 00:08:28,627
revoke the old one,

233
00:08:28,627 --> 00:08:30,001
rotate it in Jenkins,

234
00:08:30,001 --> 00:08:30,655
and build.

235
00:08:31,205 --> 00:08:32,848
The link is in the description.

236
00:08:34,398 --> 00:08:35,273
Your turn.

237
00:08:35,823 --> 00:08:40,196
One: make a project analysis token, with a name and an expiry date.

238
00:08:40,746 --> 00:08:45,589
Two: prove it is small. Ask an administrator question with it, and see it refused.

239
00:08:46,139 --> 00:08:51,323
Three: revoke your old token, run your pipeline, and see it fail with not authorized.

240
00:08:51,873 --> 00:08:57,206
Four: put the new token in the Jenkins credential, and run it again, until it is green.

241
00:08:57,756 --> 00:09:00,401
Five: run lab check, and get four of four.

242
00:09:00,951 --> 00:09:02,679
Pause the video, and do it now.

243
00:09:18,229 --> 00:09:19,104
Quick check.

244
00:09:19,654 --> 00:09:21,723
Which token type should a pipeline use?

245
00:09:22,273 --> 00:09:23,852
What does least privilege mean?

246
00:09:24,402 --> 00:09:26,428
What happens when you revoke a token?

247
00:09:26,978 --> 00:09:29,880
Where is the token stored, and where is it never stored?

248
00:09:30,430 --> 00:09:35,486
Objective covered: M C eighteen, objective seven. Tokens and permissions.

249
00:09:36,036 --> 00:09:38,105
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

250
00:09:48,655 --> 00:09:52,282
Next: how to diagnose a failing pipeline, step by step.

251
00:09:52,832 --> 00:09:56,160
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
